Z||000000||chris6878||11-02-1999||12:45 PM||||Hey Guys..<P>What is the estimated cost of a Basic V8 swap. The basic kit from archies is $850...<P>How much more should this swap run me.. not counting the engine and the kit...  just other odds and ends..      coult this be achieved under $1500 (US dollars)<P>Thanks Guys/Gals...<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Eric Marsh||11-02-1999||01:44 PM||||So you question is, is it possible to spend less than $650 for the additional parts that are not included in Archie's basic kit? Off the top of my head, here is a list of the parts you will need. Prices are loose and fast and I'm assuming you will purchase from a discount house such as Summit Racing:<P>Remote oil filter and adaptor: $75<BR>Remote electric water pump (I assume this is pre-'88): $175 (I think Archie's remote drive is about $250).<BR>Radiator hoses and stuff: $75<BR>Misc small parts: $50<BR>New trans mounts: $60<BR>Flywheel and clutch - Don't know. Is this an automatic or manual? For an automatic you can figure $75 for the flexplate. Manual clutch may be significantly more.<BR>Throttle cable mount: $35<BR>Exhaust (cheapest) $100<BR>Starter motor: $225<P>Like I said, this is just off the top of my head. Looks like its gonna cost more than $650.<P>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||11-02-1999||02:15 PM||||Thanks Eric...||||reg||6
